.TH DB-ACTIVITY 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
 db-activity \- bounded, read-only SQL session activity and lock hints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B db-activity --engine postgresql|mysql|mariadb
.RI [ --host " HOST" ]
.RI [ --port " PORT" ]
.RI [ --database " NAME" ]
.RI [ --user " NAME" ]
.RI [ --client " ABSOLUTE_PATH" ]
.RI [ --defaults-file " ABSOLUTE_PATH" ]
.RI [ --timeout " 1..30" ]
.RI [ --min-seconds " 0..86400" ]
.RI [ --limit " 1..100" ]
.RI [ --include-idle ]
.RI [ --null ]
.br
.B db-activity --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queries native PostgreSQL, MySQL or MariaDB clients using fixed, read-only SQL.
No statement text, client IP addresses or password command-line arguments are
retrieved or printed. The own diagnostic connection is excluded.
No sessions are killed; no locks are released.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --engine
One of postgresql, mysql, mariadb.
.TP
.B --host, --port, --database, --user
Connection target and database identity options; port requires host.
Explicit TCP requires verified TLS; absent host forces MySQL/MariaDB socket.
.TP
.B --client
Absolute path to a native command-line client executable.
.TP
.B --defaults-file
Absolute regular private mode-0600 MySQL/MariaDB client options file.
Only credential and TLS file options in [client] are allowed.
.TP
.B --timeout
Native client connection timeout, 1 to 30 seconds (default 5), plus bounded process runtime.
.TP
.B --min-seconds
Minimum reported activity/state age, 0 to 86400 (default 0).
.TP
.B --limit
Maximum output session count, 1 to 100 (default 25).
A query requests at most limit+1 for truncation detection; truncation returns 1.
.TP
.B --include-idle
Include MySQL/MariaDB Sleep and PostgreSQL idle sessions.
.TP
.B --null
Ten NUL-delimited fields per record, no header. Check the exit code for truncation.
.SH OUTPUT
Tab-separated ENGINE, SCOPE, SESSION_ID, DB_USER, DATABASE, STATE, SECONDS,
WAIT, LOCK_STATUS, BLOCKERS. PostgreSQL requires pg_read_all_stats for full
cluster activity. Its pg_blocking_pids count gives a momentary blocker count;
state waiting may have no reported blockers. MySQL/MariaDB PROCESSLIST state
provides possible lock hints only and BLOCKERS is ?. Without PROCESS privilege
MySQL/MariaDB show only sessions visible to the current account.
SECONDS semantics differ between backends; consult the detailed guide.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful complete snapshot, including empty result.
.TP
.B 1
Database/permission failure or incomplete result (server had more than limit rows).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid invocation.
.TP
.B 3
Missing prerequisite, timeout, malformed or oversized client output.
.SH NOTES
Raw SQL statement text is deliberately excluded. MySQL's INFORMATION_SCHEMA
PROCESSLIST is deprecated upstream. These reports are snapshots, not a
complete blocker graph, deadlock detector or continuous monitor.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR db-probe (1),
.BR db-health (1),
.BR psql (1),
.BR mysql (1),
.BR mariadb (1)
.SH DOCUMENTATION
See docs/commands/db-activity.md and db-activity.de.md.
